<title>UK: London tea auction sees fair demand.</title>
<headline>London tea auction sees fair demand.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Landed teas were in fair demand and offshores saw good comeptition at the latest auction held by the Tea Brokers' Asociation of London.</p>
<p>The few bright East Africans on offer were 4 to 6 pence easier. Mediums also declined up to 8 pence. Plainer descriptions remained firm.</p>
<p>Among offshores, Central Africans were irregular and sometimes dearer but Kenyas moved lower.</p>
</text>
